From d52f7164fa2132c1da8f3fb77cd6ef160d6f6ef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohi <noelrohi59@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 02:13:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] skua #17: draw finished layers early (bounded blend-layer
 textures); render census; runtime in-flight bound

WgpuCommandHandler kept every trivial/complex blend's stage-sized layer texture alive until the
parent command list was fully chunked (N sibling layers = N full-stage textures). The handler now
draws the pending chunks onto its target after every layer_flush() layers (SKUA_LAYER_FLUSH,
default 8, 0 = upstream), so the pool reuses a handful of textures. Not done for a Layer's own
surface, whose target nested Alpha/Erase blends read while it is still being chunked.

Also: per-frame counters (skua_render_census), set_max_in_flight/max_in_flight.
---
 render/wgpu/src/backend.rs          |  94 ++++++-
 render/wgpu/src/buffer_pool.rs      |   1 +
 render/wgpu/src/surface.rs          | 412 +++++++++++++++-------------
 render/wgpu/src/surface/commands.rs | 110 +++++++-
 4 files changed, 424 insertions(+), 193 deletions(-)

